  "verbalization": "Pramipexole is associated with the Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through a chain of indications that link it to Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, which in turn is indicated by Cycrimine, Entacapone, and Istradefylline. This suggests a potential pathway where Pramipexole may influence the development of this syndrome through its interaction with these medications. The evidence indicates that Pramipexole could be a contributing factor in the pathogenesis of the syndrome, possibly through mechanisms involving dopamine receptor modulation or other pharmacological effects. The overlapping indications suggest a possible role of Pramipexole in the pathophysiology of the syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The strength of the evidence is supported by the consistent scores across the three paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a direct or indirect relationship between Pramipexole and the syndrome.",
